with Penny's late husband, Martin Spector. You could say Martin was an idea man. He worked in advertising. And if you're picturing the life of a New York ad executive filled with cocktails, like brain storming and Madison Avenue glamour, go right ahead. In the 1950s and 60s Martin wrapped some of the biggest names in publishing, such as barons, dow Jones, and the Wall Street Journal. And we ate dinner out most evenings and Martin got some of his best ideas, just jotted down in the backs of Olden, Velopes as everybody did.
故事的主人公是彭尼已故的丈夫马丁·斯佩克特。你可以说马丁是一个充满点子的人。他从事广告工作。如果你脑海中浮现出纽约广告高管的生活，充满鸡尾酒、头脑风暴和麦迪逊大道的魅力，那就尽管想象吧。在20世纪50年代和60年代，马丁为出版业的一些最大巨头处理过业务，比如巴伦周刊、道琼斯和《华尔街日报》。我们几乎每天晚上都在外面吃晚餐，马丁的一些最好的灵感，就像大家常做的那样，只是随手记在旧信封的背面。

