Can you hear me now? Can you hear me now? Can you hear me now? God, milk. And not just any questions, but excited questions, exclamatory questions. Questions like... Wesson! Wesson!  without placing question marks and exclamation points back to back. Spectre saw that in this case, the ancient model of reading still held.
你现在能听到我说话吗？你现在能听到我说话吗？你现在能听到我说话吗？天哪，牛奶。而且不仅仅是普通的疑问句，而是激动的疑问句，感叹式的疑问句。像这样的疑问句……Wesson！Wesson！……却无法将问号和感叹号背靠背地放在一起。斯佩克特发现，在这种情况下，古代的阅读模式依然适用。

