If you wrote an exclamatory question, the reader was still expected to work out the nature of the sentence through context, not punctuation. Then we were having dinner one night when he came up with a solution for it. The interrebang. Spectre was the editor of a typography magazine called Type Talks. And in the March, April 1962 issue, in an article titled Making a New Point, or How About That, he proposed the first new end mark in the English language in 300 years. With the Interro Bang, Spectre collapsed the question mark and the exclamation point into
如果你写了一个感叹式的疑问句，读者仍然需要通过上下文来琢磨句子的性质，而不是靠标点符号。然后有一天我们在吃晚餐时，他想出了一个解决方案。疑问感叹号（interrobang）。斯佩克特曾是一本名为《Type Talks》的排版杂志的编辑。在1962年3月/4月号上，在一篇题为《创造一个新标点，或者觉得这怎么样》的文章中，他提出了300年来英语中的第一个新句末标点。通过疑问感叹号，斯佩克特将问号和感叹号融合成

12
00:05:43.000 --> 00:06:24.000
a single glyph. The two marks instead of being placed placed back to back, were now conjoined, sharing the same dot at the bottom of the line, with the sharp vertical slash of the exclamation point nestled inside the sinuous curve of the question mark. The inter-bang means exactly what it looks like. It notes a question that expresses surprise or incredulity. This also makes it useful for rhetorical questions, most of which are it turns out also incredulous. In his article, Spectre was already envisioning exclamatory slash rhetorical advertising slogans that could take advantage of this new mark, such as what a refrigerator that makes its own ice cubes, although
了一个单一的字形。这两个符号没有背靠背地放置，而是结合在了一起，共享行底部的同一个圆点，感叹号尖锐的垂直斜线嵌套在问号优美的曲线之中。疑问感叹号的意思和它的外表完全一样。它表示一个表达惊讶或怀疑的疑问句。这也使得它非常适合用于修辞疑问句，事实证明，大多数修辞疑问句也带有怀疑色彩。在文章中，斯佩克特已经在构想可以利用这个新符号的感叹式/修辞式广告标语，比如，竟然有能自己做冰块的电冰箱，尽管

