There's irony mark invented by a kind of Renaissance man called John Wilkins who had proposed an inverted exclamation mark and it went nowhere. And then there's the interrobe, which seemingly from the day it was born, faced a string of bad luck. For example, an article praising the interrobe appeared in the New York Carol Tribune in 1962, after the writer at Red Martin's original piece in type talks. In the Tribune article, the writer called the intero-bang true genius. But unfortunately, his article was published on the 1st of April, and readers may have took it as an April Fools joke. So there's that little blip.
还有由一位名叫约翰·威尔金斯的文艺复兴式全才发明的讽刺号（irony mark），他曾提议使用一个倒过来的感叹号，但它最终不了了之。然后还有疑问感叹号（interrobang），似乎从它诞生的第一天起，就遭遇了一连串的好运不济。例如，一篇赞美疑问感叹号的文章于1962年在《纽约先驱论坛报》上发表，此前该报的撰稿人阅读了马顿在《Type Talks》上的原创文章。在这篇《论坛报》文章中，作者称疑问感叹号为真正的天才。但不幸的是，他的文章发表在4月1日，读者们可能把它当成了一个愚人节玩笑。所以，这就是一个小插曲。

18
00:08:44.000 --> 00:09:12.000
Still our baby punctuation marked persevered. In 1966 a company called the American Type Founders, a legendary design firm that created some of the most widely used typefaces of the 20th century, unveiled a new typeface called Americana that included an Interro bag. And then the company slowly went bust. Americana was the last font they actually cut, and so they did not cut anymore in TerroBanks. But all was not lost.
尽管如此，我们这个初生的标点符号还是坚持了下来。1966年，一家名为美国铅字铸造公司（American Type Founders）的传奇设计公司——该公司创造了20世纪一些使用最广泛的字体——推出了一种名为Americana的新字体，其中就包含了一个疑问感叹号。然后这家公司就慢慢破产了。Americana是他们实际雕刻的最后一款字体，因此他们再也没有雕刻过更多的疑问感叹号。但并不是一切都失去了。

19
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:39.000
In the year 1968, the iconic typewriter company Remington announced that their latest model typewriter would feature an optional in TerroBank key. But I wonder if perhaps the fact that you had to pay some extra money to get an in terobank key might have turned people off. Today, the in terobank is just barely hanging in there. The mark is recognized by websters, just like Penny said, and it is included in a surprising number of computer fonts.
在1968年，标志性的打字机公司雷明顿（Remington）宣布，他们最新型号的打字机将配备一个可选的疑问感叹号键。但我想，也许是因为你必须支付额外的费用才能买到一个疑问感叹号键，这件事可能把人们吓退了。如今，疑问感叹号只是勉强维持着存在。正如彭尼所说，这个符号得到了韦伯斯特词典的认可，并且它被收录在数量惊人的计算机字体中。

20
00:09:39.000 --> 00:10:08.000
It even has its own character in Unicode, the common directory of symbols which all computer fonts must reference. But Keith points out that it still hasn't cleared the biggest typographical hurdle of all. I think that to consider it to be a real mark of punctuation, people have to use it without thinking about it. In other words, a truly remarkable mark of punctuation must be unremarkable. It must be banal. And banality is not one of the interobeying strong suits.
它甚至在统一码（Unicode）中有自己的字符，而统一码是所有计算机字体都必须参考的通用符号目录。但基斯指出，它依然没有跨越最大的排版障碍。我认为要把它视为一个真正的标点符号，人们必须在不假思索的情况下使用它。换句话说，一个真正杰出的标点符号必须是毫不起眼的。它必须是平庸的。而平庸并不是疑问感叹号的强项。

21
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:37.000
After Remington's brief attempt to give it a key, it never made it onto any standard keyboards. And now, if it is included in a font, it's accessible only with an inestated series of menus and selections. So when people do use it, they're deliberately going out of their way to do so. They're using it because it's fun, not because it's needed. Keith has gone on to document ever more outlandish examples of the intero-bang, which have, perversely, only made it stand out more, further undermining its legitimacy.
在雷明顿短暂尝试为其添加一个按键之后，它就再也没有进入任何标准键盘。现在，如果它被包含在某个字体中，只能通过一系列嵌套的菜单和选项才能访问它。因此，当人们使用它时，他们是刻意绕道而行才这么做的。他们使用它是觉得好玩，而不是因为需要。基斯接着记录了更多关于疑问感叹号的奇葩例子，这些例子反而适得其反，让它更加显眼，进一步削弱了它的合法性。

22
00:10:37.000 --> 00:11:07.000
A quick Facebook search yields at least two bands named Intero-bang, one punk, one brass. In 2014, an Australian cartographer in the state of Victoria painted an InteroBang on the roof of his house. It's now visible on Google Maps. And in 2017, the Minneapolis Star Tribune ran an obituary for the poet J. Otis Powell, who had always ended his name with an exclamation point, but changed it to an InteroBang before his death. None of these examples are in the service of an exclamatory question.
在Facebook上快速搜索一下，至少能找到两个以“Interrobang”命名的乐队，一个朋克乐队，一个铜管乐队。2014年，维多利亚州的一位澳大利亚制图师在他家的屋顶上画了一个疑问感叹号。现在在谷歌地图上还能看到它。2017年，《明尼阿波利斯明星论坛报》为诗人J·奥蒂斯·鲍威尔刊登了一则讣告，他的名字总是以感叹号结尾，但在去世前，他将感叹号改成了疑问感叹号。这些例子都不是为了表达感叹式的疑问。

