for ordinary people to employ the intero-bang, for no other reason, beyond the fact that the sentence at hand calls for its use. Maybe then we can say that it's made it, maybe then we can say that it's made it. Maybe then we can say that it's a real market punctuation. This left me with only one question. Have you ever seen any truly earnest, truly banal in terabangs in the wild, so to speak? Who knows?
即普通人在使用疑问感叹号时，没有别的原因，纯粹是因为当下的句子需要它。也许到了那个时候，我们才能说它成功了，也许到了那个时候，我们才能说它成功了。也许到了那个时候，我们才能说它是一个真正的标点符号。这只留给我一个问题。你有没有在野外——可以这么说——见过任何真正真诚、真正平庸的疑问感叹号？谁知道呢？

